{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q855654","formula":"C₁₉H₂₀FN₃","hill":"C19H20FN3","elements":["H","C","N","F"],"composition":{"C":19.0,"F":1.0,"H":20.0,"N":3.0},"names":{"en":"Fluperlapine"},"descriptions":{"en":"Fluperlapine (NB 106-689), also known as fluoroperlapine, is a morphanthridine (11H-dibenzo[b,e]azepine) atypical antipsychotic with additional antidepressant and sedative effects. It was first synthesized in 1979, and then subsequently studied in animals and humans in 1984 and beyond, but despite demonstrating efficacy in the treatment of a variety of medical conditions including schizophrenia, psychosis associated with Parkinson's disease, depressive symptoms, and dystonia, it was never marketed. This was perhaps due to its capacity for producing potentially life-threatening agranulocytosis, similarly to clozapine, which it closely resembles both structurally and pharmacologically."},"fame":5,"pubchemCid":49381,"mass":309.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CN1CCN(CC1)C2=NC3=C(CC4=CC=CC=C42)C=CC(=C3)F","inchikey":"OBWGMKKHCLHVIE-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"3-fluoro-6-(4-methylpiperazin-1-yl)-11H-benzo[c][1]benzazepine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"49381","atoms":43,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":4.714,"y":-2.649,"z":-1.21,"el":"F"},{"x":-1.775,"y":-0.731,"z":0.448,"el":"N"},{"x":-4.548,"y":-1.323,"z":0.16,"el":"N"},{"x":0.478,"y":-1.19,"z":0.42,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.203,"y":-2.103,"z":0.178,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.773,"y":0.108,"z":1.111,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.537,"y":-2.101,"z":-0.571,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.094,"y":0.063,"z":0.341,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.487,"y":-0.321,"z":0.261,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.299,"y":1.118,"z":-0.108,"el":"C"},{"x":0.704,"y":1.896,"z":0.491,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.829,"y":-1.357,"z":-0.544,"el":"C"},{"x":1.679,"y":1.287,"z":1.462,"el":"C"},{"x":2.487,"y":0.218,"z":